Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:35:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway, provider: a conversation's compaction writer is
 found by the stable id its rename keeps (#2642)

What changed: compactions.json recorded the writer's name alone, and
every match for it went by the name: checkpointReaders among the
candidates, checkpointGone among the logins. A Codex account's name is
not stable - a Team seat reads "email . Team", and a second seat of one
email reads "email . Team . workspace" (#1424) - so a conversation
sealed before the account's name changed was refused with "X is no
longer signed in to magpie" though it was signed in all along, under its
new name, and the recovery the message gives, signing in again, changed
nothing (ScarfQian, #2642, on v0.1.1285; the same false guidance as the
"switched off" refusal of an account that was on). The record now
carries the account's stable id beside its name (checkpointWriter.ID,
the logins' #905), wroteCheckpoint takes it from the candidate
(provider.AccountID), and both matches go by either (isWriter,
checkpointGone): a renamed writer gets its conversation still, and a
gone one's refusal says what the settings now say of its new name.
What kept the id from serving this till now is fixed with it:
rememberLogins replaces a saved record with the sign-in read from the
agent, which carries no id, and upsertLogin's replace kept Order, On and
Paused but let the id go - writeLogins stamped it anew from the name, so
the id moved whenever the name did. The record's id is kept now, and a
fold of two records of one account takes whichever has it
(dedupeLogins).

Run at this change (parent ccb2eea1):
- go test -tags nogui -count=1 -run TestNativeCompactionWriterRenamed
  ./internal/gateway/ and -run TestLoginIDKeptThroughALiveSignIn
  ./internal/provider/: red on the parent (the gateway one with the
  reporter's refusal, "me@example.com is no longer signed in to
  magpie"), green here.
- go test -tags nogui -p 2 ./internal/provider/: ok, 74.657s.
- go test -tags nogui -p 2 -timeout 45m ./internal/gateway/: ok,
  328.238s.
- go test -race -tags nogui -run TestNativeCompactionWriterRenamed and
  TestLoginID over both packages: ok.
- gofmt -l over both: clean. go vet -tags nogui over both, darwin,
  linux, windows: clean. go build -tags nogui darwin and linux,
  GOOS=windows: ok (the known trayimage cgo warning on darwin).

Ablation and mutation, tests kept: the three product files back to the
parent, all three tests red again; logins.go alone back, the renamed
conversation refused again and the provider test red; the id match out
of isWriter (signature kept), the renamed conversation refused again;
the id match out of checkpointGone, the refusal reads "no longer signed
in" again. Each restored, green.

